note={cited By 0; Conference of 29th International Conference Information Visualisation, IV 2025 ; Conference Date: 5 August 2025 Through 8 August 2025;  Conference Code:215222},
url={https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105024534497&doi=10.1109%2fIV68685.2025.00026&partnerID=40&md5=a7182c746080df226574bc5fe3c90f60},
affiliation={Universidade NOVA de Lisboa, ICNOVA, Lisbon, Portugal; Lusófona University, CICANT, Lisbon, Portugal},
abstract={The spread of animation in education and science communication has substantially increased due to the technical developments of the last decades. While educational animation is an increasingly well-mapped field, a communication gap still exists between visual storytellers and scientists. This paper addresses that gap by proposing guided discussion points to support effective interdisciplinary collaboration. Drawing on Communication Models and Communication Design Principles, two initial key stages of collaborative production are identified: (1) Project Identification, wherein Communication Theory informs the extraction and framing of the scientific core to be visualized in a cross-cultural communication framework, and (2) Project Description, where definitions from the field of Multimedia Learning and principles from Communication Design guide the visual articulation of scientific content, complemented with case studies of science animation categorization and online examples to highlight discussion points in practice. The parallel processes inherent in both animation production and scientific research provide a comparative framework for mutual understanding, serving as a foundation for dialogue that recognizes scientists and visual storytellers as equal partners in co-creating compelling and accurate science visualizations. © 2025 IEEE.},
author_keywords={animation;  explainer videos;  interdisciplinary collaboration;  science communication;  science visualization},
keywords={Computation theory;  Multimedia systems;  Visual communication;  Visualization, Audio-visual;  Communication design;  Communication gaps;  Communications modeling;  Explainer video;  Interdisciplinary collaborations;  Modeling designs;  Science communications;  Science visualization;  Technical development, Animation},
